/**
   @page dum_main The Dialog Usage Manager library (dum)

   The Dialog Usage Manager (DUM) sits on top of the @ref resip_main "SIP stack"
   as its resip::TransactionUser, and gives applications a much higher-level
   API for building SIP user agents and servers. DUM tracks dialogs and
   dialog sets, generates requests and responses with the correct headers,
   handles authentication challenges, refreshes registrations and
   subscriptions, and runs the INVITE offer/answer state machine. It does no
   media handling; see @ref recon_main for that.

   @section dum_concepts Concepts
      - Usages : Each thing an application does over SIP is a usage, with a
      client side and a server side: resip::ClientInviteSession and
      resip::ServerInviteSession (calls), resip::ClientRegistration and
      resip::ServerRegistration, resip::ClientSubscription and
      resip::ServerSubscription (SUBSCRIBE/NOTIFY and REFER),
      resip::ClientPublication and resip::ServerPublication,
      resip::ClientPagerMessage and resip::ServerPagerMessage (MESSAGE), and
      resip::ClientOutOfDialogReq and resip::ServerOutOfDialogReq (OPTIONS
      and other requests outside a dialog).
      - Handles : Applications refer to usages through handles, such as
      resip::InviteSessionHandle and resip::ClientRegistrationHandle (see
      Handles.hxx). A handle can outlive its usage; check isValid() before
      using one that was stored.
      - Handlers : Applications learn about events by implementing handler
      interfaces, such as resip::InviteSessionHandler,
      resip::ClientRegistrationHandler, resip::ClientSubscriptionHandler,
      resip::ServerSubscriptionHandler and resip::OutOfDialogHandler, and
      registering them with the resip::DialogUsageManager.
      - Profiles : resip::MasterProfile holds the settings for the whole DUM
      (supported methods, MIME types, options tags and so on), and
      resip::UserProfile holds per-user settings such as the From address,
      digest credentials and registration time. Most make functions accept a
      resip::UserProfile, and use the master profile when one is not given.
      - Application dialog sets : Subclass resip::AppDialogSet and
      resip::AppDialog, and set a resip::AppDialogSetFactory, to attach
      application state to each dialog set and dialog.

   @section dum_usage Usage
      - Create a resip::SipStack and add transports to it (see
      @ref resip_usage).
      - Create a resip::DialogUsageManager for the stack.
      - Give it a resip::MasterProfile with
      resip::DialogUsageManager::setMasterProfile().
      - Add a resip::ClientAuthManager, to answer digest challenges, and, on
      the server side, a resip::ServerAuthManager.
      - Register your handlers with the set...Handler() and add...Handler()
      functions.
      - Start usages with the make functions, such as
      resip::DialogUsageManager::makeInviteSession(),
      resip::DialogUsageManager::makeRegistration() and
      resip::DialogUsageManager::makeSubscription(), and pass the request
      they return to resip::DialogUsageManager::send().
      - Give DUM processing cycles, either by calling
      resip::DialogUsageManager::process() in a loop after
      the stack's process(unsigned int timeoutMs), or by running a resip::DumThread
      alongside the stack's own thread.
      - Shut down with resip::DialogUsageManager::shutdown(), which reports
      completion through resip::DumShutdownHandler.

      resip/dum/test/basicRegister.cxx is a short, complete example, and
      basicClient (basicClientUserAgent.cxx and basicClientCall.cxx in the
      same directory) is a fuller user agent.

   @section dum_threads Threads
      DUM is not thread-safe. Handlers are called from the thread that runs
      resip::DialogUsageManager::process(), and the application must call
      DUM, and use handles, only from that thread. To act from another thread,
      post a resip::DumCommand to the resip::DialogUsageManager; its
      executeCommand() runs on the DUM thread.

   @section dum_extending Extending DUM
      - resip::DumFeature : Plug-in processing for incoming and outgoing
      messages, added with resip::DialogUsageManager::addIncomingFeature()
      and resip::DialogUsageManager::addOutgoingFeature().
      - resip::RegistrationPersistenceManager : Storage for registrations
      received by resip::ServerRegistration.
      resip::InMemoryRegistrationDatabase keeps them in memory, and
      resip::InMemorySyncRegDb also supports replicating them to a peer
      server (repro uses it for registration sync).
      - resip::KeepAliveManager : Sends periodic keepalives to the servers the
      application talks to, keeping connections and NAT bindings open.
*/
